int debug_remove_breakpoint(int id);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes a breakpoint from the debugger\(cqs linked list by its numeric
ID.
The breakpoint\(cqs \f[CR]pattern\f[R] and \f[CR]condition\f[R] strings
are freed, and the breakpoint node itself is freed.
.PP
The linked list is traversed using a pointer\-to\-pointer technique for
efficient removal without special\-casing the head node.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]id\f[R] \(em The breakpoint ID to remove.
This is the value returned by \f[CR]debug_add_breakpoint()\f[R] when the
breakpoint was created.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success (breakpoint found and removed).
.PP
Returns \-1 if no breakpoint with the given ID exists.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]debug_add_breakpoint\f[R](3),
\f[CR]debug_list_breakpoints\f[R](3), \f[CR]debug_cleanup\f[R](3)
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Removing all breakpoints does \f[B]not\f[R] automatically deactivate
debug mode or unregister the hook.
The hook remains registered to support step\-mode execution even without
breakpoints.
Use \f[CR]debug_cleanup()\f[R] to fully deactivate.
.IP \(bu 2
The breakpoint ID is not recycled; subsequent calls to
\f[CR]debug_add_breakpoint()\f[R] will use the next sequential ID.
